            <ArticleTitle>Discovery of pyrazolopyrimidine derivatives as novel inhibitors of ataxia telangiectasia and rad3 related protein (ATR).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>750-754</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(17)30058-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2017.01.045</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The ATR pathway is a critical mediator of the replication stress response in cells. In aberrantly proliferating cancer cells, this pathway can help maintain sufficient genomic integrity for cancer cell progression. Herein we describe the discovery of 19, a pyrazolopyrimidine-containing inhibitor of ATR via a strategic repurposing of compounds targeting PI3K.</AbstractText>
